diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c239667..5584fc9 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -197,6 +197,7 @@ anusint/
 | Symptom | Likely cause / fix |
 |---|---|
 | `rate_limited_try_again_later` | You're hitting Instagram too fast — raise `--delay`, or wait a bit before retrying. |
+| `instagram_requires_login_for_this_profile` (HTTP 401) | **This is not a bug.** As of 2026, Instagram has been progressively gating the logged-out `web_profile_info` endpoint on a growing share of accounts — it can return 401 even with correct headers, no prior requests, and a clean IP. There is no reliable public-data-only fix for this: the remaining workarounds (authenticated-session scraping, browser-fingerprint impersonation with residential proxies) are deliberately out of scope for this project — see [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). If you hit this, verify the profile manually in a browser instead. |
 | `unexpected_response_format_endpoint_may_have_changed` | Instagram changed their internal response format (this isn't an official public API). Run the URL in `config.WEB_PROFILE_URL` manually and update the field mapping in `profile_snapshot.fetch_public_profile()`. |
 | `connection_error` / `timeout` on every request | Check your network, or a proxy/firewall may be blocking outbound HTTPS. |
 | Colors look like garbled `\033[...]` text | Your terminal doesn't support ANSI color, or output is being piped/redirected — add `--no-color`. |
